                <td style="padding: 12px 18px; font-size: 0.95rem;">Must be neutralized with sodium hydroxide or triethanolamine (TEA) to pH 7.0–8.5. Synergizes with non-ionics to lower CMC.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr style="border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);">
                <td style="padding: 12px 18px;"><strong>Non-ionic &amp; Amphoteric Surfactants</strong><br/><span style="font-size:0.85rem; color:var(--text-muted);">C12-15 Ethoxylates (9EO), CAPB</span></td>
                <td style="padding: 12px 18px; font-size: 0.95rem;">Grease emulsification, foam stabilization, skin mildness</td>
                <td style="padding: 12px 18px; font-size: 0.95rem;">Insensitive to water hardness. CAPB acts as an amphoteric hydrotrope, boosting viscosity and stabilizing dense foam structures.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr style="border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);">
                <td style="padding: 12px 18px;"><strong>Chelating Agents</strong><br/><span style="font-size:0.85rem; color:var(--text-muted);">Tetrasodium GLDA, Tetrasodium EDTA</span></td>
                <td style="padding: 12px 18px; font-size: 0.95rem;">Water softening, calcium/magnesium ion sequestration</td>
                <td style="padding: 12px 18px; font-size: 0.95rem;">GLDA is preferred for bio-based, phosphate-free compliance. High thermal stability and excellent binding kinetics in alkaline systems.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr style="border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);">
                <td style="padding: 12px 18px;"><strong>Rheology Modifiers</strong><br/><span style="font-size:0.85rem; color:var(--text-muted);">Carbomers, Xanthan Gum, NaCl electrolyte</span></td>
                <td style="padding: 12px 18px; font-size: 0.95rem;">Viscosity adjustment, yield value development, particle suspension</td>
                <td style="padding: 12px 18px; font-size: 0.95rem;">Salt-thickening works for SLES/CAPB complexes. Polymeric thickeners are required for acid toilet cleaners or to suspend abrasive particulates.</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
